    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) standing as our premier play. Facing a favorable 4.80 xERA matchup against Ober, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an optimal leadoff spot and a 5% wind-aided boost, but the true catalyst is his elite sprint speed against a slow-working pitcher, creating an ideal environment for his primary value-add: stolen bases. **Christian Yelich** (74.22) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) follow closely as high-confidence starts. **Christian Yelich** leverages a strong platoon advantage batting at the top of the order, while **Kazuma Okamoto** benefits from a porous 4.67 xERA matchup against Kay, providing a high floor for our core production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Junior Caminero** (58.95) and **Chase Meidroth** (34.47). While **Junior Caminero** holds the UTIL spot despite a difficult matchup against Rivera, he narrowly edged out the rest of the bench. **Chase Meidroth** was our primary consideration for the final slot, but his projection plummeted due to a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult 3.33 xERA matchup, ultimately landing him well below our 40-point efficiency floor. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (56.17); while his 0.475 xwOBA remains elite, the unfavorable matchup against a 3.23 xERA pitcher suppresses his efficiency score compared to his typical ceiling. **Casey Schmitt** also presents a situational risk, as his matchup against Miller, B\u2014a pitcher with a sub-3.00 xERA\u2014significantly dampens his utility today. With **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** off today, the Zebras rely on the high-contact upside of our current starters to maintain our standing in the 5x5 race.",
